# ARK Market Authority

**Full document:** [docs/ecosystem/ark-market-authority-v1.md](../../docs/ecosystem/ark-market-authority-v1.md)

**Frozen 2026-07-07.** Do not extend v1 Growth Pressure / ledger code without realigning to this model.

## Naming

**Market Authority** = trust the market grants the business (business health).

**Authority** elsewhere in ARK = DDD operational truth (`RepairOrder`, `Vehicle`, …).

**Earned Authority** = publication gate when knowledge leaves the shop — different job. See [ark-earned-authority.mdc](ark-earned-authority.mdc).

## Three frozen statements

**Law:** Operational excellence creates market authority opportunities. Markets determine whether those opportunities become market authority.

**Corollary:** Businesses control opportunities and investments. Markets control outcomes.

**Becoming (meta-principle):** Every projection exists to answer: *What is becoming true?*

## Non-negotiable causal chain

Successful repair → **Opportunity Created** (not gated on review ask) → investments (invitation, ads, …) → market witnesses (review, referral, return, …) → observations → projections.

**Businesses cannot grant market authority to themselves.** Market authority is inferred, never a table or score.

## Advisor vs model

Advisor UI: *"Did you invite the customer to share their experience?"* — not doctrine vocabulary.

Model events: `MarketAuthorityOpportunityCreated`, `MarketAuthorityInvestmentMade`, market witnesses later.

## Before measuring outcomes

**Never measure an outcome until the opportunity that produced it is identified.** Count reviews last; ask when trust was possible first.

## Do not

- Gate opportunity on review checkbox
- Treat ledger/score as truth
- Gamify capture rate
- Build Selection Pressure before repeated floor vocabulary
